  "instructions": [
    "Toss the turkey strips in a bowl with the Chinese five-spice powder until evenly coated.",
    "Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Add the seasoned turkey and cook for 3 to 4 minutes, stirring frequently, until lightly browned.",
    "Add the ginger, sugar snap peas, and bok choy to the skillet. Cook for 2 to 3 minutes, stirring constantly, until the vegetables turn bright green.",
    "Pour the chicken broth, rice vinegar, and low-sodium soy sauce into the pan. Simmer for 1 to 2 minutes, tossing well, until the turkey is cooked through and the sauce lightly coats the ingredients.",
    "Heat the brown rice pouch in the microwave for 1 to 2 minutes until steaming hot.",
    "Divide the warm brown rice between two plates. Top evenly with the turkey and vegetable stir-fry, then garnish with the toasted sesame seeds."
